1261:  *      ninth until the stub learned to return 2):
1262:  *        re-arm `> 32768' -> `>= 32768'       EQUIVALENT: at 32768 both assign 32768
1263:  *        re-arm `> 32768' -> `> 32767'        EQUIVALENT: the same
1264:  *        arm `> 32768' -> `>= 32768'          EQUIVALENT: the same
1265:  *        arm `> 32768' -> `> 32767'           EQUIVALENT: the same
1266:  *        either clamp written with 32768L     EQUIVALENT: the same values
1267:  *        arm clamp operand -> data_in_len     EQUIVALENT: atapi_len was assigned it one line up,
1268:  *                                             and data_in_len (a size_t of at most 64 MiB,
1269:  *                                             SCSI_MAX_XFER_BYTES) converts to int exactly
