171: 
172: `while (inbuf_len < 0)` (`dev_wdc.c:1650-1651`) is data flow into `inbuf_len == 12`, not a guard. `<= 0`, `< -1` and deletion pass every row: (e). The reason is not "a CDB never wraps". Reachable inside one CMDOUT: `ATAPI_PKT_CMD`, then 262655 times a 1-byte DATA store and a 1-byte DATA read (both pointers sit at 262655; `WDC_INBUF_SIZE` is `512*(512+1)` = 262656, `dev_wdc.c:47-48`), then twelve 1-byte zero stores. HEAD normalises `head - tail = 11 - 262655` to 12 and dispatches (occupancy 0, COMPLETED, ireason `0x03`). Deletion leaves the local count negative (occupancy 12, CMDOUT, ireason `0x01`) (`codex_r3pass_records.txt:83-93`). Not rowed. `<= 0` and `< -1`: the drain ANNOUNCE arm at `dev_wdc.c:1881-1885` has no `!badlen_this` term and can differ for `WDCC_WRITEMULTI` with `write_count >= 2` after an unimplemented-width store on an empty ring. Host latch `warned_empty_drain` only (fable `fable5_r3pass.md:112`).
