80: - o2_re_ne: `received <= data_in_len` is an invariant at HEAD -- the arm sets received 0 and `atapi_len = min(data_in_len, 32768)` (:1779-1795); each read moves `consumed` from `atapi_len` to `received` (:1293-1294) with `consumed <= atapi_len` (:1290); each re-arm sets `atapi_len = min(data_in_len - received, 32768)` (:1424-1428); a CMDOUT stray read runs only the move; a new PKT changes neither; the dispatch re-bases received.  So `!=` is `<` on every reachable state.  (The equivalence is fragile -- it rests on #475 -- which is exactly why the contract names #475 beside it; fine.)
81: - o2_re_len0_le: `atapi_len` never negative at HEAD given #475 and the arm's bound (above).
82: - E_nlen0_le1: (count 1, st NULL) unreachable -- :1735 is the only writer of `atapi_st`.
83: - o1_ri_bitor / p2_I1: at every reachable refill `received` is a multiple of 32768 (a shorter chunk is the LAST chunk: `received == data_in_len` at its end, so the `<` arm is not re-entered) and `j < 32768`, so `|`/`^` equal `+`.
84: - p2_R5 (re-arm's `PHASE_DATAIN` store deleted): the `<` arm is entered only in DATAIN at HEAD -- in COMPLETED `received >= data_in_len` always (the completion, the reject arm's 0/0, the no-data arm's 0/0, the zero-length cell after its read), and in DATAOUT `data_in_len` is 0 because both `return 2` paths (:888-892 WRITE, :1287-1291 MODE SELECT) allocate `data_out` only and the dispatch's `atapi_st` is fresh (:1735).  AGREE.
85: - p2_S3 (reject arm's `received = 0` deleted): every `return 0` precedes any allocation (:282-327, before the opcode switch), so a rejected command's fresh transfer is (NULL, 0) and `received < 0` is false for any received.  AGREE.
