101: 3. The CDB-opcode compare `scsi_cmd[0] == READ_CAPACITY || READ_10 || MODE_SENSE10` (:1747-1750), which sets `cmd_len = 10`: a statement on the dispatch path between the guard and the arm (both outcomes reach the edit, so not a dominator and not floor), but guest-visible -- `diskimage_scsicmd.c:573` switches on `cmd_len` for MODE SENSE and reads the allocation length from bytes 7-8 only when it is 10; drop the MODE_SENSE10 term and a MODE SENSE(10) is served the length in byte 4 -- and INVISIBLE to this detector by construction: the stub never reads `cmd_len`.  It belongs in the OUT-OF-CONTRACT list, stated.
