123: 
124: Yes as a pass: the diff was delivered (26 hunks inlined, matching the frozen file), every premise in section 2 was checkable from the packet plus the frozen artifacts and the pinned commit (all checked above; none refuted -- the N3 premise's READ TOC path is READ at diskimage_scsicmd.c:1161-1169, `device.c:265` defaults `addr_mult` to 1, the PIO fixture is right against :1472-1476, the disabled read returns zeros through :2050-2066 and skips :2048), the roster is the coordinator's to state, and the denominator is stated above.  But a valid pass that finds a breach does not close the chain: the stop condition is "the FIRST PASS THAT FINDS ZERO BREACHES", and this one finds one member of the (d) enumeration -- a clause-(2) operand swap on a predicate the contract itself lists as dominating -- that passes all 159 rows by reading and is guest-reachable by routine traffic, plus one survivor whose (e) grade rests on reading the compare's own input as "the flow".  REPAIR4 is one row (plus, if the VD1 dispute is upheld, one line in an existing row), and the class to write into the contract this time is the OPERAND-SWAP axis of every dominating guard -- both flag guards were walked for their branch partition and only one of them for its swaps.
